course/modules/PC/PC3/L01.html:408:              <p>The printed reduction for quote updates is 0.9163 and the baseline total is 2.9704. Dividing those four-place values gives 0.3085, which is 30.85 percent and would round to 30.9 percent, so the solution divides the full-precision values instead. The full-precision quote-updates reduction is 0.9162907319 and the full-precision baseline is 2.9704144656, and their quotient is 0.308472, which is 30.8 percent to one decimal place. The minutes reduction is 0.1753528875, and its quotient with the same baseline is 0.059033, which is 5.9 percent. The share base in both cases is the baseline total width of Lab 1, Part 2.</p>
(end)
